---
import { withBase } from "../../../site.config.mjs";
---

<section class="pi-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="pi-install-title">
  <p class="pi-kicker">After the download</p>
  <h2 id="pi-install-title">Install in a couple of minutes</h2>
  <div class="pi-grid pi-grid--three">
    <article class="pi-card">
      <h3>Windows</h3>
      <p>
        Run the NSIS installer and open Pi Desktop from the Start menu. The portable .exe needs no
        install.
      </p>
      <p class="pi-warning">
        Unsigned build. If SmartScreen appears, choose <strong>More info → Run anyway</strong>.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="pi-card">
      <h3>macOS</h3>
      <p>
        Open the .dmg and drag Pi Desktop into <code>/Applications</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="pi-warning">
        The build is unsigned and not notarized. Launch once, then open
        <strong>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security</strong> and choose
        <strong>Open Anyway</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The .zip is for the updater; install from the .dmg. Updates are manual until the app has a
        stable signing identity.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="pi-card">
      <h3>Linux</h3>
      <p>Make the AppImage executable and run it, or install the .deb:</p>
      <pre><code>chmod +x Pi-Desktop-*.AppImage
./Pi-Desktop-*.AppImage

sudo apt install ./Pi-Desktop-*.deb</code></pre>
      <p class="pi-warning">
        AppImage needs FUSE (<code>libfuse2</code>) or <code>--appimage-extract-and-run</code>. Use{" "}
        <code>apt install ./file.deb</code>, not <code>dpkg -i</code>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="pi-section__more">
    Full steps, data locations and the first-run flow:
    <a href={withBase("/guide/getting-started/")}>Getting started</a>.
  </p>
</section>
